nixpkgs: nixos-26.05 (see flake.lock; unchanged from 0/1/2)
changes: First version of series 0.2, prompted by the first real nixos-anywhere install (agenthub). (1) Passwordless wheel sudo: security.sudo.wheelNeedsPassword = false hardcoded in the base — 0/1 hosts had no path to root by construction (key-only users with locked passwords, sshd key-only, root login disabled; nothing can ever satisfy the sudo prompt; only the provider rescue console worked). NOPASSWD for wheel is the only coherent policy under key-only auth (D-015). (2) bnox.users accounts now explicitly locked: hashedPassword = mkDefault "!" — was implicit; now self-documenting and immune to upstream default changes. A host's own hashedPassword/password still wins by documented NixOS precedence. Zero behavior change today. (3) bnox-nats-stream-init could never succeed on any host: the stream config JSON omitted num_replicas (natscli --config applies no defaults → every stream add rejected with "must be >= 1 but found 0"), and the update path prompted for confirmation without a TTY (and would have zeroed the -1 "unlimited" limits to 0). Config is now complete/explicit (durations as ns), update passes --force, and update failures no longer count as success. Verified end-to-end against the pinned nats-server 2.12.3 + natscli 0.3.0; fresh hosts no longer boot degraded. (4) Series docs: nixos-anywhere Ubuntu-target recipe (cpio prerequisite, --kexec-syscall for unsigned kexec images on 7.x kernels, run detached) and passwordless-sudo note. Verified on agenthub (repin + rebuild + fresh boot): is-system-running = running, stream-init active (exited) with the stream created, passwordless sudo served by the bnox base.
